        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. What to know from the first round of France's municipal elections France Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 15:59 In France's municipal elections the far right National Rally is gaining momentum, and France Unbowed has made a breakthrough. Both parties, which treated the municipal elections as a test-run for the presidential race, emerged strengthened from the first round, in a vote that generally saw the left hold its ground, particularly in Paris, Marseille, and Lyon. Here’s an overview of the key takeaways. Former president Sarkozy appeals conviction in Libyan funding case 16/03/2026 France 44% abstention: French local elections 'poorly attended dress rehearsal' for 2027 presidential race 16/03/2026 France Paris looks at five-way race for new mayor 16/03/2026 France Far-right and left make major gains across France in mayoral election 16/03/2026 France Voter turnout reaches 48.90% in France's first round of local elections 15/03/2026 France French parties test strategies in municipal elections ahead of 2027 presidential poll 15/03/2026 France Trial over 2014 Air Algeria plane crash opens in Paris 09/03/2026 France Middle East war: Fuel prices surge in France amid margin concerns 06/03/2026 France Macron says France is sending its aircraft carrier to the Mediterranean 03/03/2026 France"
