        "link": "https://www.france24.com/en/trump-administration-threatens-media-over-middle-east-war-coverage",
        "orario": "15:52",
        "timestamp": 1773672734,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump administration threatens media over negative coverage of Middle East war Americas Issued on: 16/03/2026 - 15:52 Modified: 16/03/2026 - 15:52 Donald Trump's broadcast regulator has issued a warning to top news channels in the United States, threatening to cancel the spectrum permits of broadcasters pushing what he called \"hoaxes and news distortions\". Brendan Carr, the chair of the Federal Communications Commission, responded to a Trump complaint about negative coverage of the Iran war. It comes amid heightened tensions between broadcasters and the FCC over how political content is handled on air. Who did the Oscars 2026 reward and honour? 16/03/2026 Culture Michael B. Jordan gets 'most thunderous applause of the night' at Oscars 16/03/2026 Culture 'One Battle of Another' wins big at Oscars 2026 as Michael B. Jordan and Jessie Buckley rewarded 16/03/2026 Americas Trump administration threatens media outlets over Iran war coverage 15/03/2026 Americas Cubans take to the streets and attack Communist Party office in rare riot over blackouts 15/03/2026 Americas She lost 5 brothers to Syria’s war – Now she’s fighting for justice at the UN 15/03/2026 Americas ICE deports Ethiopian national who called for violence on social media 14/03/2026 Americas Cuba begins releasing prisoners and confirms US talks as island's energy crisis intensifies 14/03/2026 Americas United States: Attack on a Michigan synagogue and deadly shooting at a Virginia University 13/03/2026 Americas"
